<title>INDIA: India Reliance 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India Reliance 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    13,230     vs    13,050</p>
<p>    Sales		   87,300     vs    77,860</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	 6.50     vs	 6.0</p>
<p>    Other income	   2,900     vs     2,720</p>
<p>    Expenditure	   70,720     vs    63,060</p>
<p>    Interest		 1,700     vs     1,100</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   4,100     vs     3,370</p>
<p>    Tax			  450     vs	NIL</p>
<p>Note - Petrochemicals giant Reliance Industries Ltd said it changed the method of calculating depreciation. Without this change the profit would have been higher by 660 million rupees, it said.</p>
<p>The company's share register will be closed from May 17 to June 14 for the dividend payment.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
